WEBVTT

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.910
What should I do?

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.120
What if I get in everyone else's way

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.660
at today's division battle...

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.700
Mr. Kannonzaka.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.500
Looks like you've got your hands full with that.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:34.830
Huh?!

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.250
"What should I do? What should I do?
What should I do? What should I do?"

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.250
Huh?!

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.910
"What should I do? What should I do?
What should I do? What should I do?"

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.910
Oh, this is...

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.330
They say you're participating
in the division battle, hmm?

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.040
Isn't that why you've been pushing your luck?

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.950
No, it's not that...

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:49.540
Get this done today.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.910
Uwahh!

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.370
Are you all right?

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.750
Sorry about that.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.250
I was in a bit of a rush.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.450
I've got to leave work on time today...

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.290
Here you go.

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:07.910
Huh?!

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.910
You're Mr. Kannonzaka, aren't you?

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.750
Today's the day of
Matenro's division battle, right?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:17.950
Uh, yeah! How did you know?

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.950
Matenro's really popular, you know?

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:21.000
Ahaha...

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.700
But I'm just the team's deadweight...

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.290
I happen to like the way you rap.

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:28.620
I think it's okay for you to
have more confidence in yourself.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.830
Confidence?

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.290
I'm Kazuha Rurikawa.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:36.200
You've just got to go to the division battle,
or else I don't know what I'd do.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.200
I can take care of the photocopying.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.450
There are people at this company
who are cheering you on, too, you know?

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.620
Th-Thanks!

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.120
♬ Listen up! (Hoo!) ♬

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.250
♬ Shout it out and keep on movin' ♬

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.830
♬ At the top of your lungs,
SAY BUS! TER! BROS! ♬

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:52.160
♬ That's right! (Hey!) ♬

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.080
♬ Give us a big Hoo (Hoo!) ♬

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.040
♬ Say Yeah (Yeah!) ♬

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:00.040
♬ We'll break past, full blast, with these voices ♬

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.660
And the winner is... Buster Bros!!!

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.700
All right! We keep this up,
and we'll make it to the finals!

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:10.450
We did it, Big Bro!

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.580
Great job, the two of you!

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:16.200
Well, it was me and Brother Ichi
who did most of the heavy lifting.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.120
Huh?!

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.540
The only reason you're in the group
is so we'd have enough bodies!

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.910
What did you say?!

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:23.000
Hmph!

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:27.540
Buster Bros!!! is in top condition.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.290
We've got Ikebukuro,

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.040
but don't we have to cover the other divisions?

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.620
Shinjuku, Shibuya, and Yokohama, huh?

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.540
We couldn't cover them all
if we went to each place in order.

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.290
All right, let's split up then.

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:42.160
I'll head to Shinjuku.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.660
I'd like to pay my respects to Dr. Jakurai.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.700
Rex, you take Shibuya.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:47.750
Here you go.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:50.500
Whoa! You're letting me take photos?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.660
Tom, you've finally recognized my talents!

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.620
I'll have 'em shaking in their boots!

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.330
Don't cause any trouble, now.

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:01.580
You can trust me, man! All right!

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.120
You sure about that?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.330
He's young. Sometimes
I let him have his own way.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:09.250
But anyhow, Iris, you cover Yokohama.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:11.700
Um, let me find you a camera, Iris...

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.910
This is all I need.
Let me borrow that other thing instead.

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:17.040
You got it.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.160
"Indomitable"

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.450
Sure enough, in this block...

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:07.450
...it appears Buster Bros!!!
is going to advance.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:13.410
We'll fuckin' slaughter them!

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.910
"Chinatown"

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.580
It's all in there.

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:26.580
Once you're through,
go to the place we agreed on

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.660
and don't make any stops along the way.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.160
It's so easy even a kid could do it,
just as long as you stick to the plan.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:33.410
A-All right.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:41.250
And the winner is... Fling Posse!

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.950
Thanks, ladies!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.620
Lady Luck's smiling on me today.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.910
Methinks the words will
flow freely from my pen today,

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.620
so with that, I bid thee farewell.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.870
I'll square my debts, you'll see!

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.330
Oh, what a bummer!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.910
I thought we'd all get something to eat.

00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:05.500
Hehehe, Ramuda's left all by his lonesome.
These'll make some great shots!

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.000
If you're gonna take pictures,
you've gotta ask first.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.120
My bad. I'm on the clock too, you know?

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:11.910
Hey.

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.160
You were at that live music club, weren't you?

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.250
I'm Taromaru Rex.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.700
Or T. Rex for short.

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.410
I'm a man with dinosaur DNA in my veins.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.950
Got myself a strange one here...

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:30.950
But the guy he was with has an incredibly
high number of views on his SNS page.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.660
Scratching his back now might pay off later.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.160
Say, as long as you're here,
won't you join me for a meal?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.370
With your dinosaur DNA and all,
perhaps you'd like a nice, juicy steak?

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.660
For real, man?

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.540
I'm a sucker for bait dangled before my eyes.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.830
Ahaha! You're such a funny guy.

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:47.750
All right then, let's get a move on!

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.040
But are you sure it's all right?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.370
Looks like your team's all
gone off to do their own thing...

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.700
Now, now,

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.080
that's nothing for you to worry about.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:06:59.870
"Matenro"

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:07.290
It's been a long time, Dr. Jakurai.

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.750
You...

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:16.750
You're the photographer who posted
that picture of Matenro on the web.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.120
Have we met somewhere before?

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.200
Yes, at a field hospital in the war zone.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:23.200
Huh?

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:25.410
I'm not surprised that you don't recall.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.620
At the time, I looked like a
mummy all wrapped up in bandages.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:32.450
I'd be dead now if you hadn't treated me.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:34.250
I see.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:36.410
I'm so glad you've recovered.

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:40.250
Matenro's been making steady wins.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.620
How's that assistant who was
with you before? Is he doing well?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:52.250
Yotsutsuji's in a coma now.

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:53.790
How did that happen?

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:59.290
In order for me to learn the truth,
I must remain undefeated.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.290
Huh?

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.500
Doctor!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.160
It's almost time for us to go on stage!

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.700
My apologies.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:07.580
We must continue our conversation another time.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:12.200
Doppo, you don't appear quite so nervous today.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.080
That's right.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.580
Something good happened to me today.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.330
I'll do my very best!

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.870
We're counting on you!

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.660
Who are you people?

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.000
"Shinjuku Central Hospital"

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.250
Well, well.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.870
It's Captain Degarashi and Detective Irihatoma.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.790
Dr. Jakurai.

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:50.450
I doubt you guys were involved in this case.

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:52.080
What do you mean, "this case"?

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:56.660
The serial burglaries that have been
happening around town these days.

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.250
The captain's in charge of the case,

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:00.790
and the fatigue's put a
lot of strain on his lower back.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:02.750
That's awful.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:07.080
Normally the captain would be trying
to make false charges against me.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.200
Yes, he would.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.200
It's just that this time there's no way
you could've been the perpetrator.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:14.500
How do you mean?

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:19.410
Huff huff...

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.080
Doppo, are you going out to make sales calls?

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.120
My boss just up and tells me
I've got to go deliver these samples.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:29.870
If I leave now to go to all these places,
it'll be nighttime before I'm done.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:31.830
I'll deliver half of them for you.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.410
No, I can't ask you to do that.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:37.080
It's no problem. You gave me a boost.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.870
Your last division battle was great.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.330
R-Really?

00:09:41.330 --> 00:09:43.580
Come on, let's do our best together!

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.830
Th-Thanks!

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:49.000
You were a real lifesaver today.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.870
I don't have a good sales
performance record, either.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:55.790
My boss has it in for me,
so I know how you feel.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:58.620
I didn't know that. In your department...

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.370
We handle endoscopes,
ultrasound machines, and other equipment.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.500
It's not my place to say this,

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.040
but you seem like a nice guy, Kazuha.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.620
Not really.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:11.540
But that boss of mine really gets me down.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:16.000
I bet he'll give me a hard time again
on the day of the next division battle.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.950
When that happens, I'll come to your rescue.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:20.750
Or should I say...

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:23.000
I won't let him do that to you.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:25.080
Th-Thanks.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:28.620
Seems like I've been saying
thanks to you this whole time.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.790
I must repay you one of these days.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.330
Doppo, you can repay me by putting
your heart and soul into Matenro.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:38.200
Is that Doppo?

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.660
Who's that with him? Could it possibly be...

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.120
Hey, Doppo!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.620
And some random guy!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:44.870
H-Hifumi!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.830
Oh, I'm so happy for you!

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.950
Doppomine, you've finally made a friend!

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:53.250
What do you mean, "friend"?

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:55.910
Oh? So, you're not friends?

00:10:55.910 --> 00:10:58.950
I'm really glad you think we are.

00:10:58.950 --> 00:11:00.450
All right!

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.000
Doppomine and some random guy!

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:04.290
Let's have a drink to celebrate!

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:05.620
"Fresh Seafood"
"Uoichi"

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:06.910
Cheers!

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:07.160
"Menu"

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.410
I'm honored.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:12.200
Who'd have thought I'd be sitting here
drinking with Matenro's Hifumi and Doppo?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:16.370
Hey, some random guy! You know about me, too?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:19.580
He's not "some random guy." His name's Kazuha.

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.500
Hifumi Izanami.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.950
Shinjuku's number one host.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:27.450
There isn't a lady in this
town who doesn't adore you.

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:28.620
A-Ahaha...

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.750
L-Ladies, huh?

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.120
What's the matter?

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.120
W-Well, let's set that
aside for the time being...

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:36.950
Right now, we're talking about Doppo!

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:40.750
Doppomine's negative
thinking is an utter black hole!

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:43.370
Because of that, the only friend he's got is me.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:44.950
That's not...

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.910
I don't have many friends, either.

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:51.250
Hehehe. You're like two peas in a pod.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:54.330
So, Kazuha, do you have
some sort of black hole, too?

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.540
I often think about where
I'd be and what I'd be doing

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:59.620
if the world was going to end the next day.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:02.700
Wow, that's pretty negative.

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.580
But, why's the world gonna end?

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:06.250
Wait? That's what you want to know?

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:07.750
So, what would you be doing?

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:11.910
Probably admiring the view
of Tokyo from Harumi Wharf.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:12.870
Why?

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.000
I was brought up on a small island.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.790
That was the place where my ship landed
when I came to Tokyo for the first time.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:20.540
Really? I'm sure you came here
with your heart full of dreams.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:25.200
I guess. But the reality is my life is dull.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.330
Actually, I've known about you
for a while now, Doppo.

00:12:28.330 --> 00:12:31.330
I heard there was someone else
like me working in a different department.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:36.700
And when I heard you'd started doing
rap battles, I thought I'd give it a try, too.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:39.370
So, is your team also participating
in the division battle?

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:42.200
Nope. We didn't even make it to the qualifiers.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.700
I see...

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.000
I'm so jealous.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.330
Doppo, you've got some good teammates

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:49.700
and found a different side of yourself.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:52.160
A different side of myself?

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:56.200
A sort of muck builds up
in every person's heart.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.580
We have to have some place
to get rid of that build-up.

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:01.700
Doppo, you've found that place.

00:13:01.700 --> 00:13:03.040
Hmm.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:05.370
I kind of get what you're saying but not quite.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:08.620
Hifumi, that's because muck
doesn't build up inside you.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:09.830
You've got that right!

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:13.500
But I'm sure you'll find it someday, Kazuha.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:18.660
Actually, I've already found a place
to release what builds up inside me.

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:21.250
Really? What is it?

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:23.500
I'll tell you someday when I'm able to.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:24.620
Okay.

00:13:24.620 --> 00:13:28.500
I'll do everything I can to support you, Kazuha.

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:29.790
Thanks.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.750
Uwahhhh!

00:13:40.870 --> 00:13:42.700
Hey, have you heard?

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:45.750
Our boss fell down
a flight of stairs and was injured.

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.750
What?! Really?

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:49.910
"Dr. Jakurai"

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:51.950
Dr. Jakurai?

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.200
"Shinjuku Central Hospital"

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:57.330
Doctor, how's my boss doing?

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:58.870
He's all right.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:01.500
He can probably be discharged
in two or three days.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.500
I'm glad to hear that.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:05.620
Doctor, I can understand
why you called Doppomine,

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.160
but what did you ask me here for?

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.500
There's something I need
to discuss with the two of you.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.790
Huh?!

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:17.540
Actually, it appears that Doppo's boss
was pushed down the flight of stairs.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.620
What? Who did it?

00:14:19.620 --> 00:14:21.790
I don't know.

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:27.620
And actually, the other day Detective Irihatoma
told me something disconcerting.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:31.330
I didn't mention it because
I didn't want to worry the two of you.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:34.290
Taken along with the current incident,
it bothers me.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.290
What's so disconcerting?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.750
The series of burglaries
that have been committed

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:41.790
with hypnosis mics around Shinjuku recently.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:44.160
Oh, I've heard about that.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:46.870
According to Detective Irihatoma,

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:51.330
the crimes have been occurring
during Matenro's division battles.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.660
In other words, the criminals
are committing the burglaries

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:58.080
while the public's attention
is focused on our battles.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.120
During our battles?

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.370
Their MO is incredible.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:05.200
They knock down the walls of the buildings.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.200
That's rather crude.

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:08.790
According to forensics,

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:11.950
the burglars stick endoscopes into the air vents

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:16.950
and use thermography and the Doppler shift to
examine the buildings' structure.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:19.040
Those are rather technical pieces of equipment.

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:22.830
They sure are.
They're also all medical equipment.

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.870
Like the ones that
Mr. Kannonzaka's company deals in.

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:30.330
So, have you heard anything
that might give us a lead in the case?

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:31.830
No, I haven't.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:33.330
I should've known.

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:36.870
I was kind of hoping I could count on you

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.040
to quickly wrap up this case
like you did last time.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.750
Ehehehehe.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:41.950
What was that?

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:44.290
The D-D-Doppo-ler shift?

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:47.790
The Doppler shift.
It's used in ultrasound machines.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.910
It's what we use to examine babies in the womb.

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:51.450
Really?

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:56.000
It's as though we've been
made accessories to the crimes.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.790
But every cloud has a silver lining, you know?

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:01.250
If the crimes hadn't
happened during our battles,

00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:03.750
Doppomine, you would've been a suspect, right?

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.080
Why do you think I'd be the only one?

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.910
Hey there, Doppo.

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:10.000
Today's the day of the division battle, right?

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.200
Isn't it great your boss is
not around to get in your way?

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.160
Huh?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:14.950
Good luck!

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:22.250
We handle endoscopes,
ultrasound machines, and other equipment.

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:26.290
You've just got to go to the division battle,
or else I don't know what I'd do.

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.370
When that happens, I'll come to your rescue.

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:31.910
I won't let him do that to you.

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:33.410
No, it can't be...

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.410
I'm sure something
will happen during this battle as well.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:41.750
We know when the crime'll happen.

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.910
The police'll take care of it somehow.

00:16:43.910 --> 00:16:47.950
But there are countless shops
in Shinjuku that could be raided.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:49.910
Clear your mind of distractions.

00:16:49.910 --> 00:16:53.450
Now is the time for us to fight.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:59.370
♬ Rollin' in hot off a car chase,
pass the mic this way ♬

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.700
♬ This is how we play and it's wicked risqué ♬

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.120
♬ We won't stand for delays,
so you better stay away ♬

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.660
♬ We are Matenro and
we're gonna make you pay ♬

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.870
♬ Rollin' in hot off a car chase,
pass the mic this way ♬

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:11.290
♬ This is how we play and it's wicked risqué ♬

00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.750
♬ We won't stand for delays,
so you better stay away ♬

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:17.330
♬ We are Matenro
and we're gonna make you pay ♬

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:22.750
So, they've struck again.

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:25.500
"Inbox 0236"
"From: Kazuha"
"I'm glad to have met you in the end. --Kazuha"

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.660
"Inbox 0236"
"From: Kazuha"
"I'm glad to have met you in the end. --Kazuha"
"I'm glad to have met you in the end."

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.080
In the end?

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:44.040
Once our ship arrives, it's goodbye to Japan.

00:17:49.450 --> 00:17:50.870
Doppo...

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:54.290
Kazuha, I figured you'd be here.

00:17:55.580 --> 00:18:00.500
You used our company's
equipment to commit burglaries.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.660
That's right.

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.200
We're the ones behind the burglaries.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.250
Was it also you who pushed
Doppo's boss down the flight of stairs?

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:08.700
He'd been a thorn in
our side in all sorts of ways.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:09.790
But why did you...

00:18:09.790 --> 00:18:12.250
Were you using me?

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.290
You said you were cheering for me.

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:16.040
Was all of that just so you
could commit burglaries?

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:20.160
Doppo, I thought you and I were alike.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.830
But we weren't.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:25.200
So, I found my own path.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:28.290
But committing burglaries? Is that really...

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:31.540
When my crimes made the news
and drew people's attention,

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.910
I thought I'd become like you once again.

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:35.700
That's not like me at all!

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:40.660
Doppo was downright ecstatic
to have made a new friend!

00:18:40.660 --> 00:18:43.040
To think you just toyed with his emotions!

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.910
Doppo, I've been wanting
to fight you for some time.

00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:50.580
Doppo, I'll let you lead us into battle.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:13.200
♬ Tell me why, baby ♬

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.500
♬ I'm just smiling like I'm solitary ♬

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.830
♬ Bros for life burst, can't have he without me ♬

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:20.620
♬ Overlapping negatives,
dark like the deep sea, yeah ♬

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:22.450
♬ Like mixin' too many colors of paint together ♬

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:23.700
♬ This situation should be makin' me high ♬

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:24.870
♬ But all I feel is low ♬

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:26.750
♬ My man, don't treat me like a piece of trash ♬

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:27.500
♬ I'm miffed, very much so ♬

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.910
♬ Threw away our peace & love a moment ago ♬

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:31.870
♬ Spit saliva on a lonely night ♬

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:34.450
♬ Every day downright idle,
my bangs shake left to right ♬

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.870
♬ The one I thought was
here at my side is out of sight ♬

00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:39.620
♬ Far away, boy, the fallen leaves taking flight ♬

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:40.790
♬ Why is it that we can't meet? ♬

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:41.910
♬ Time is up, forgive me ♬

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.200
♬ Plan out your identity ♬

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:44.700
♬ Believe in yourself ♬

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.540
♬ Clinking a glass to toast your burning spirit ♬

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.370
♬ I believe your dark past will light up ♬

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.580
♬ Leaves scattered over this
dilemma are colors of the rainbow ♬

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:53.080
♬ Giving up and crying at the evening's start ♬

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.370
♬ Sleepy eyes on the platform
waiting for the 5AM train ♬

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:57.910
♬ Secretly, the fluttering of my heart ♬

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:00.290
♬ I'm not strong but even
I can find the beat and blow ♬

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:02.830
♬ Bare all, brother, help me in my rewrite ♬

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:04.080
♬ You're saying you have hopes for them? ♬

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:05.500
♬ Once again, I'll pull out my umbrella ♬

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:08.870
♬ Recalling memories, "Who are you?" ♬

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:13.790
Uwahhhhhhh!

00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:20.500
Kazuha, why did you contact me?

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:24.450
When you sent that email, you must've
known we'd figure out where you were.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:29.580
Somewhere deep down,
you must've regretted what you'd done.

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.250
And you sought Doppo's help.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.910
When I arrived here for the first time,

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:37.580
the view from here was glittering.

00:20:39.540 --> 00:20:43.500
But today the view was dark and dull.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:45.660
I've become tainted.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:49.620
Thank you, Doppo, for saving me.

00:20:49.620 --> 00:20:51.370
You poor fool...

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:00.080
We are in your debt.

00:21:00.080 --> 00:21:03.040
Once again you guys solved our case.

00:21:03.040 --> 00:21:06.580
Kazuha and I were
no different from each other...

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.790
No, you're wrong about that.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:11.450
He lacked imagination.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.910
Imagination?

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:15.370
The ability to put himself
in someone else's shoes.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:18.580
And the ability to believe in himself.

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:20.790
If you keep on acting selfish,

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:23.120
you're bound to hurt somebody once in a while.

00:21:23.120 --> 00:21:25.250
But you don't do stuff like that.
Right, Doppomine?

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:28.000
Hifumi... Doctor...

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.410
And the winner is... MAD TRIGGER CREW!

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:39.450
Everything went according to plan.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:41.250
That was an easy win.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.700
The qualifiers ain't no big deal.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.790
Crime in progress in Kannai, Naka-ku.

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:56.290
Suspect is armed and on the run.

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.950
All nearby officers report
to the scene immediately.

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:01.370
I'm sorry. This is urgent.

00:22:01.370 --> 00:22:03.290
I've got to go now.

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:07.620
Did something go down?

00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:09.660
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:10.290
What do you mean?

00:22:10.290 --> 00:22:13.700
Depending on the case,
Jyuto may be roped in to the investigation.

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:17.410
In other words, he won't be able
to participate in tomorrow's battle.
